<h2 id="shard-of-the-throne" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Shard%20of%20the%20Throne">Shard of the Throne</a> (removed in Prophecy of Kings)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This agenda is removed from the game when playing with Prophecy of Kings.<sup>8</sup></li>
    <li>If the <i>Shard of the Throne</i> law is discarded, no player loses a victory point.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>Shard of the Throne does not change hands if a combat ends in a draw, or if no combat occurs, such as when ground forces land on a planet without opposing ground forces or the Bombardment ability destroys the last defending ground forces.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="shared-research"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Shared%20Research">Shared Research</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; outcome is resolved, a player with no command tokens in their reinforcements does not place one. They do not take a command token from their command sheet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the &ldquo;Against&rdquo; outcome is resolved, a player places the command token in their home system even if they control no planets there.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="swords-to-plowshares"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Swords%20to%20Plowshares">Swords to Plowshares</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a planet contains only one infantry, that infantry is destroyed and its owner gains one trade good. All trade goods from Swords to Plowshares are gained together, so the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may use their Pillage faction ability on each affected neighbor only once.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Mechs are ignored by the &ldquo;For&rdquo; effect of <i>Swords to Plowshares</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Neutral infantry are unaffected by <i>Swords to Plowshares</i>, as there is no neutral player.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

